## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical API testing skills for real-world payments: idempotency, webhooks, and concurrency.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent operations and Idempotency-Key
- External payment provider mocking and webhook handling
- Retry/backoff strategies and race-condition testing
- End-to-end flow verification with minimal flakiness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-test for idempotent checkout
test('idempotent checkout creates single order', async () => {
  const key = 'abc123';
  const res1 = await POST('/checkout', {items:[1,2,3]}, {headers: {'Idempotency-Key': key}});
  const res2 = await POST('/checkout', {items:[1,2,3]}, {headers: {'Idempotency-Key': key}});
  expect(res1.status).toBe(200);
  expect(res2.status).toBe(200);
  expect(res2.body.id).toBe(res1.body.id);
});
```

